What is the difference between:
1. A) Spline – A referral to a nurse who works with children and young people in their own homes;
2. Placement – A referral to a child’s school or community, where they are allowed to receive services outside of the school, for example by contacting the school or local authority;
3. Placement – An appointment to a child’s school or community and/or school or school district;
4. Placement – A placement to a child’s school or community or school district to help them learn how to use and understand English.
The nurse is an adult at the time the child is born, but he/she has been called to the hospital (usually at home). As the child grows, the nurse is also required to be present for the first 6 months of life.
It can take some time for the nurse to get his/her attention, but it may be a good idea to see if you can help him/her find the best place for herself.
